  <main_text>
    <p><i>Origo rerum: nescia Principum</i></p>
    <p><i>Sperare Regem, nescia credere,</i></p>
    <p><i>Vero, potenti, nostra proteruitas.</i></p>
    <p><i>Hac caterorum femina criminum,</i></p>
    <p><i>Hunc fas reatum dicere seculi:</i></p>
    <p><i>Iustus malorum luxuriantium</i></p>
    <p><i>Fons Ynde, &amp; omnis causa periculi.</i></p>
    <p><i>Dedere lustris anterioribus</i></p>
    <p><i>Hac nempe Gallum talia pracinem,</i></p>
    <p><i>Illum, parentis munus Olympici.</i></p>
    <p><i>Egressa priscum qua penitus modum</i></p>
    <p><i>Nunc nunc Britannus, nunc Latialibus,</i></p>
    <p><i>Nunc Lusitanis, nunc Calydoniis,</i></p>
    <p><i>Et Vltimarum denique gentium</i></p>
    <p><i>Egent cothurnis. Viuite perpetes</i></p>
    <p><i>Par grande Vatum, Viuite, Viuite:</i></p>
    <p><i>Piaque cinKti tempora laurea</i></p>
    <p><i>Verum sacratis ISACIVM modis</i></p>
    <p><i>Effere. Lauri non alia magis</i></p>
    <p><i>Amoliantur fulmina Calitum.</i></p>
    <head level="1">IAC. LECTIVS</head>
    <p>T 4</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Scan is faded and speckled; the words "Ynde", "cincti" and "Effere" are read with some doubt. The head line may be a printed title and the "T 4" a signature-like mark.</notes>
